    "help.start.title": "Getting started",
    "help.start.body": "Ether has no accounts and no central server that stores your messages. When you first open the app, you pick a name and a phone number or email — this is only used to generate your private identifier (a hash), the actual phone/email is never sent anywhere. To talk to someone, you both need to add each other as contacts: by typing their phone/email, by scanning their QR code, or by them sharing their contact card with you.",
    "help.contacts.title": "Adding contacts",
    "help.contacts.body": "Go to the Contacts tab and enter the other person's phone or email, or tap \"My QR code\" to show your own code for them to scan, or \"Scan QR code\" to scan theirs. You can also forward a contact you already have to someone else directly from a chat. Contacts added this way (QR, forwarding, or through a group) won't show a phone/email in their profile — only their name and identifier — that's expected, not a bug: the raw contact info is never transmitted this way.",
    "help.messaging.title": "Sending messages",
    "help.messaging.body": "Type in the box at the bottom and send. Swipe a message left (or open its menu) to reply to it, copy it, edit or delete your own messages, or forward them to someone else. Long-press or tap a message to react with an emoji. If a message failed to send, tap it and choose \"Retry\".",
    "help.media.title": "Photos, files and voice messages",
    "help.media.body": "Tap the paperclip to attach a photo, video or any file (up to 15 MB). Tap the microphone icon to record a voice message — release to send. Files and voice messages only send while you and the other person are both online at the same time (a live connection) — the server does not store attachments, only short text messages get an offline delivery queue.",
    "help.disappearing.title": "Disappearing messages",
    "help.disappearing.body": "Open a contact's profile and set a timer (1 hour, 1 day or 1 week). Every message sent after that will delete itself locally, for both of you, once the timer runs out. Turning the timer off only affects new messages — anything already sent will still disappear on schedule.",
    "help.groups.title": "Group chats",
    "help.groups.body": "From the Contacts tab, tap \"New group\", give it a name and pick up to 9 people. Groups work by connecting you directly to every other member (up to 10 people total) — there's no group server. Calls, files, voice messages and disappearing timers aren't available in groups yet; text messages, replies and forwarding work normally.",
    "help.calls.title": "Voice and video calls",
    "help.calls.body": "Tap the phone or camera icon at the top of a chat to call. During a call you can mute your microphone, turn your camera on or off, flip between front and back camera, and switch between the earpiece and speaker. Calls only work while both people are online — there's no voicemail or offline callback.",
    "help.privacy.title": "Privacy and security",
    "help.privacy.body": "Messages are end-to-end encrypted — only you and the other person can read them, not the server. The server only helps two devices find each other and briefly holds an encrypted envelope if the recipient is offline. You can set a PIN code in Settings to lock the app when it's not in use; this only hides the screen from a casual glance, it does not add extra encryption to what's already stored on your device.",
    "help.settingsHelp.title": "Settings",
    "help.settingsHelp.body": "In Settings you can change your display name, interface language, and appearance (light, dark or automatic). You can also turn sounds, notifications and link previews on or off, and export or import a backup of your contacts and messages. Advanced diagnostic tools are hidden by default — tap the \"Settings\" title at the top of this screen 5 times to reveal them.",
